  "instructions": [
    "Rinse the rice in a fine strainer until the water runs mostly clear. Add it to a medium pot with the water and salt.",
    "Bring the rice to a boil, then cover and reduce the heat to low. Cook for 15 minutes, then turn off the heat and let it steam, covered, while you cook the chicken.",
    "Stir the soy sauce, oyster sauce, fish sauce, and brown sugar together in a small bowl until the sugar dissolves.",
    "Heat the oil in a 12 inch skillet over high heat until it shimmers. Add the chicken in a single layer and cook for 4 minutes, stirring once or twice, until browned in spots.",
    "Add the garlic, chiles, and bell pepper. Stir fry for 2 minutes until the garlic is fragrant and the pepper is just tender.",
    "Pour in the sauce and cook for 1 to 2 minutes, until it coats the chicken and the chicken reaches 165 F in the thickest pieces.",
    "Turn off the heat and stir in the basil until just wilted, about 30 seconds.",
    "Fluff the rice with a fork and divide it among four bowls. Spoon the chicken and sauce over the top."
  ],
